joularcore=0.0.1: Library to monitor hardware components' energy consumption on all OSes
Origin: commit 51506dca1a84e4252002fa0af78897933fb76fd3 from https://github.com/joular/joularcore.git
Properties:
   Author: Adel Noureddine
   Description: Library to monitor hardware components' energy consumption on all OSes
   GPR Scenario: JOULARCORE_LIBRARY_TYPE := static | relocatable | static-pic
   GPR Scenario: PJ_OS := linux | windows | macos | bsd
   case OS is
      when Freebsd => GPR External: PJ_OS := bsd
      when Linux => GPR External: PJ_OS := linux
      when Macos => GPR External: PJ_OS := macos
      when Windows => GPR External: PJ_OS := windows
   License: LGPL-3.0-only
   Long_Description: Joular Core measures the energy or power consumption of hardware components:
CPU (Intel and AMD through RAPL on Linux and Windows, Raspberry Pi and other
boards through power models) and GPU (Nvidia through NVML, AMD through hwmon
sysfs or ADLX). It detects on its own what the machine offers, and also
provides a C interface so any language with a C FFI can use it.

   Maintainer: Adel Noureddine <adel.noureddine@outlook.com>
